  "Each new western territory reopened the question of whether slavery could spread, and the compromises of 1820 and 1850 only postponed the conflict. "
  "When Abraham Lincoln, whose party opposed slavery's expansion, won the 1860 election, eleven Southern states seceded. "
  "The war that followed killed an estimated 620,000 to 750,000 soldiers and ended slavery. During Reconstruction, Black men voted and held office. Then white Southern governments imposed Jim Crow segregation, which lasted into the 1960s.",
