dict(id="china", short="China's century of humiliation", title="China's 'Century of Humiliation'", span=[1793,1997], region="as",
 summary="In 1793 the Qing emperor told Britain that China needed nothing from it. Fifty years later, British gunboats forced China to accept the opium trade and hand over Hong Kong. "
  "What followed is remembered in China as the 'century of humiliation'. The Taiping Rebellion became the deadliest civil war of the 19th century, with perhaps 20-30 million dead. More unequal treaties followed, then defeat by Japan in 1895 and a scramble by foreign powers for ports and railways. "
  "The anti-foreign Boxer uprising of 1900 ended with eight foreign armies in Beijing. The Qing dynasty fell in 1911, and after 1916 China split among rival warlords. "
  "Nationalists and Communists fought each other and Japan, which seized Manchuria in 1931 and invaded China in 1937. The Communists won in 1949. Hong Kong's return in 1997 closed the circle.",
 chapters=[("Opium and rebellion",1793,1864,"The Opium Wars and the Taiping."),
           ("Carved like a melon",1865,1910,"Defeat by Japan, foreign concessions and the Boxers."),
           ("Republic, warlords and invasion",1911,1949,"The Qing falls; Japan invades; the Communists win."),
           ("Epilogue",1950,1997,"Hong Kong returns.")],
 items=["China rebuffs British trade mission","First Opium War","Treaty of Nanjing","Taiping Rebellion","Summer Palace burned","First Sino-Japanese War",
        "Treaty of Shimonoseki","Russia takes Port Arthur","Boxer Rebellion","Qing dynasty falls","May Fourth Movement","Chinese Civil War begins",
        "Japan seizes Manchuria","Japan invades China","People's Republic of China","Hong Kong returned; Asian Financial Crisis"],
 links=[("China rebuffs British trade mission","First Opium War","Britain bought vast amounts of Chinese tea but could sell China little except smuggled Indian opium. When the Qing cracked down on the drug, Britain went to war."),
  ("First Opium War","Treaty of Nanjing","Defeat forced China to pay an indemnity, open five ports and hand over Hong Kong."),
  ("Treaty of Nanjing","Taiping Rebellion","Defeat discredited the Qing, and the war's disruption of trade and jobs in south China fed the Taiping uprising."),
  ("Taiping Rebellion","Summer Palace burned","With the Qing fighting the Taiping, Britain and France pressed new demands in the Second Opium War and burned the emperor's Summer Palace in 1860."),
  ("Summer Palace burned","First Sino-Japanese War","After 1860 the Qing tried 'self-strengthening', buying modern ships and guns. In 1894 Japan's more thorough modernisation destroyed them."),
  ("Russia takes Port Arthur","Boxer Rebellion","The 1897-98 scramble for concessions, including Germany's seizure of Qingdao and Russia's of Port Arthur, inflamed anti-foreign anger in north China."),
  ("Boxer Rebellion","Qing dynasty falls","A huge indemnity and the occupation of Beijing destroyed what was left of Qing prestige. Revolutionaries gained support, and the dynasty fell in 1911."),
  ("Qing dynasty falls","May Fourth Movement","The new republic collapsed into warlord rule. When the Versailles conference gave Germany's rights in Shandong to Japan, students rose in protest."),
  ("Treaty of Versailles","May Fourth Movement","News that the Allies had handed Shandong to Japan, not back to China, sparked the protests of May 4, 1919."),
  ("May Fourth Movement","Chinese Civil War begins","May Fourth radicals founded the Chinese Communist Party in 1921. The Nationalists turned on their Communist allies in 1927."),
  ("Qing dynasty falls","Japan seizes Manchuria","A China divided among warlords could not resist when Japanese officers staged the Mukden Incident in 1931."),
  ("Japan seizes Manchuria","Japan invades China","From Manchuria, Japan pushed into north China; a clash at the Marco Polo Bridge in 1937 became all-out war."),
  ("Japan invades China","People's Republic of China","War with Japan exhausted the Nationalists while the Communists grew from about 40,000 members in 1937 to 1.2 million by 1945."),
  ("Chinese Civil War begins","People's Republic of China","After Japan's defeat the civil war resumed; the Communists won in 1949 and the Nationalists fled to Taiwan."),
  ("Treaty of Nanjing","Hong Kong returned; Asian Financial Crisis","The island ceded in 1842 returned to China after 155 years.")],
 reading=["Jonathan Spence, The Search for Modern China (3rd ed., 2013)","Stephen Platt, Imperial Twilight (2018) and Autumn in the Heavenly Kingdom (2012)",
          "Julia Lovell, The Opium War (2011)","Rana Mitter, Forgotten Ally: China's World War II, 1937-1945 (2013)"]),

